<article class="env-lemma" id="0H9B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H9B">Lemma <span data-tag="0H9B">28.30.9</span>.</a> Let $U$, $V$ be affine schemes and let $W \to U$ and $W \to V$ be open immersions. For any $w \in W$ there exists an affine open neighbourhood $W' \subset W$ of $w$ such that $W'$ maps to a standard open of both $U$ and $V$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $X$ be the glueing of $U$ and $V$ along $W$ and apply Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01IW" data-tag="01IW">26.11.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>